    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d372-a1">

                <pb facs="0698" n="602" sameAs="frus:frus1874/pg602"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No.
                    280.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <p>The secretary of state for finances and commerce gives notice to the
                    administrators of the republic that a new piece of American money, called the
                    trade-dollar, has just been introduced into this country, where it circulates
                    for one dollar specie.</p>
                <p>This piece not being comprised in the schedule of moneys compared with the
                    European dollar (<hi rendition="#italic">a la piastre d’Europe</hi>) to serve
                    for the collection of taxes to be made in the treasuries of the republic, every
                    treasurer must refuse to accept it in the collection of duties or other taxes
                    which he will have to make until the legal standard or the intrinsic value of
                    this new money be definitively fixed.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
